        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. A look back at French former first lady Bernadette Chirac's legacy France Issued on: 06/06/2026 - 16:37 Bernadette Chirac, the steel-willed former first lady of France who spent 12 years at the Élysée Palace from 1995 to 2007 beside President Jacques Chirac – weathering his notorious infidelities with dry humor while building her own political power base in rural France – has died. She was 93. FRANCE 24's Philip Turle breaks down her legacy. Bernadette Chirac, former first lady of France, dies aged 93 06/06/2026 France Former French first lady dies at 93: Bernadette Chirac, a 'discreet force' 06/06/2026 France 'Judicial system should believe victims first', activist says after body found in missing girl case 04/06/2026 France A year before the French election, De Gaulle remains politically fashionable 03/06/2026 France Under Paris's Notre Dame, archaeologists are unearthing 2,000 years of history 03/06/2026 France 1994 Tutsi Genocide: 'French government has never fully come to terms with its involvement' 02/06/2026 Africa Russian oil tanker intercepted by France and allies in Atlantic 01/06/2026 RUSSIA France mourns intellectual 'grandfather', sociologist and philosopher Edgar Morin 30/05/2026 France \"Choose France\" summit to kick off as factory closures multiply 30/05/2026 France"
